1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A supplier outage has left a fictional automotive plant
six thousand coolant pumps short.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
The line stops in forty-seven hours. Which approved backup
can actually commit capacity today?

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,000
CapacityLine is a commitment-recovery system
for the procurement team that owns this exposure.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
It starts with authorized suppliers and buyer-controlled rules:
quantity, date, price, certification, origin, and authority.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
One recovery sprint creates parallel,
goal-driven CALL-E conversations.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The live path uses the official server SDK, strict results,
transcript evidence, and idempotency.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
This accelerated path makes no calls.
Live mode requires authorized numbers and explicit confirmation.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:58,000
CALL-E returns comparable commitments—not just summaries.
Two suppliers qualify; one is short and late.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:08,000
One does not answer, and one looks best on speed and price.
The control loop waits for the buyer instead of guessing.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The command center recommends Kanto's exact-part commitment
and calls out the cheaper offer it refused.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Delta is faster and cheaper, but cannot establish IATF.
Facts come from conversation; policy fails uncertainty closed.

12
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Kanto passes all eight guardrails. The buyer can inspect
supporting words, authority, confidence, and conditions.

13
00:01:47,000 --> 00:02:02,000
A human approves an RFQ handoff.
CapacityLine never places an order or forms a contract.

14
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:11,000
The product measures Time to First Qualified Fallback:
launch to the first complete option that passes every hard rule.

15
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Every answer is transcript-grounded; no answer stays unknown.
The exposure is modeled—not claimed savings.

16
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:29,000
This is not a one-off automotive phone bot.
The same recovery loop ships with six operating playbooks.

17
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:38,000
MRO, construction, food and packaging, logistics,
and stockout recovery reuse the same authority model.

18
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Lean teams start from an approved list; enterprises add identity,
regional policy, integration, and reconciliation.

19
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Each tenant builds a private commitment graph.
CapacityLine: recover a verified commitment before operations stop.
